#POC 2 — API-Connected Application (User Catalogue)
Context: learning to interact with a backend (other than Drupal).
Objective: create an Angular application connected to an API (e.g., weather, products, users).

##To build:
Call a public API (e.g., users)
Display a list of users (name, email, city)
Add: user detail page, refresh button, error handling (API down)

Technical context: HttpClient + RxJS, service → component architecture.

Expected deliverables: functional app with dynamic data, loading/error handling, clear service/API separation.

Estimated effort: 3–4 days

Technical challenges: HttpClient usage, API calls (GET / POST), RxJS / Observables intro, error handling.

What this builds: ability to work in a modern architecture, API-driven development, base for real client projects.